{
  "id": "COMPOUND:32952 - PROTEIN:5943",
  "verbalization": "Chiricanine A is implicated in the regulation of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Chiricanine A acts as a target of CPC-N, which in turn is a target of Ganoderic Acid Tr, and both CPC-N and Ganoderic Acid Tr are targets of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP. This indicates a potential regulatory relationship where Chiricanine A may influence the activity of the phosphatase through its interaction with CPC-N or Ganoderic Acid Tr. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Chiricanine A could modulate the phosphatase activity, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a network of targets that ultimately converge on the phosphatase, suggesting a broader role for Chiricanine A in the regulation of this enzyme.",
